 4: Warehouse Inventory Reconciliation

 Compare opening stock, received stock, dispatched stock, and recorded closing stock for products. Report any mismatch and calculate the quantity needed to reach a target stock.

  Algorithm

1. Start.

2. Create product records as a list of lists.

3. For each product, calculate expected closing stock.

4. Compare expected and recorded closing stock.

5. Calculate shortage relative to target stock.

6. Display the results.

7. Stop.


. Flowchart 

( START )
    ↓
[Read product stock details]
    ↓
[Calculate expected stock]
    ↓
◇ Expected stock = recorded stock? ◇
  Yes ↓                    No ↓
[Print stock matches]   [Print discrepancy]
          ↓                  ↓
       [Calculate shortage / replenishment]
                    ↓
             / Display results /
                    ↓
                 ( END )

   Python Code

products = [

    ["Pens", 100, 50, 30, 120, 150],

    ["Books", 80, 20, 25, 70, 100],

    ["Files", 40, 10, 5, 45, 50]

]

 

for item in products:

    name, opening, received, dispatched, recorded, target = item

    expected = opening + received - dispatched

    shortage = target - expected

 

    if shortage < 0:

        shortage = 0

 

    print("\nProduct:", name)

    print("Expected closing stock:", expected)

    if expected == recorded:

        print("Status: Stock matches")

    else:

        print("Status: Discrepancy")

        print("Recorded closing stock:", recorded)

    print("Quantity to reach target:", shortage)

